title: Dashboard › Filters › Pick a date range
route: /dashboard?from=2026-10-05&to=2026-10-12
intro: The calendar at the right end of the filter bar, after 'Outcomes for'. Pick a first day, then a last day, then Apply. The range only changes the figures in Payers at a glance.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Dashboard is open\n'Outcomes for' and a date button, e.g. 'Sep 21 – Oct 20, 2026'"
click c1 "Click the date button"
process p1 "Calendar starts from the range that is applied\nTwo months show: Sep 2026 and Oct 2026"
overlay o1 "Calendar pop-up\nShortcuts on the left, two months, 'Cancel' and 'Apply'"
toast t0 "Footer shows 'Sep 21, 2026 to Oct 20, 2026'\n'Apply' is ready (it re-applies the same range)"
process p2 "Days after today are dimmed and cannot be clicked\nThe right arrow stops when the next month starts after today"

click c2 "Click a first day, e.g. Oct 5"
toast t1 "Footer: 'Start Oct 5, 2026. Now pick an end day.'\n'Apply' is disabled"
process p3 "Moving the mouse over days shades the range as a preview"
click c3 "Click a second day"
decision d1 "Is the second day on or after the first?"
process p4 "That day becomes the new first day\nStill waiting for an end day"
process p5 "That day becomes the last day"
toast t2 "Footer: 'Oct 5, 2026 to Oct 12, 2026'\n'Apply' is ready"
click c4 "Click a day when a first and last day are already set"
process p6 "Starts again: the day becomes the first day and the last day is cleared"

click c5 "Click 'Apply'"
store w1 "Filter 'range' saved: Oct 5 to Oct 12"
process p7 "Calendar closes\nThe date button shows 'Oct 5 – Oct 12, 2026' and turns green and bold"
process p8 "Address gets ?from=2026-10-05&to=2026-10-12\nThe default last 30 days leaves no from or to"
process p9 "Table goes back to its first 8 rows"
screen sc "Payers at a glance\n'Denied (8 d)' and 'Info asks (8 d)' rescale to 8 days\n'Approved as asked' shifts slightly"
process p10 "Not changed: headline, stage tiles and requests table"

click c6 "Click 'Cancel'"
click c7 "Press Escape, click outside, or click the date button again"
end e1 "Calendar closes\nThe draft is thrown away and the applied range stays"
end e2 "Range applied"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Date range shortcuts, keys and the address"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Payers at a glance › Read the table and pick a payer"

s1 --> c1 --> p1 --> o1 --> t0
o1 --> p2
t0 --> c2 --> t1 --> p3 --> c3 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| p5 --> t2
d1 -->|No, an earlier day| p4 --> c3
t2 --> c4 --> p6 --> c2
t2 --> c5
c5 --> w1 --> p7 --> p8 --> p9 --> sc --> p10 --> e2
sc --> g2
o1 --> c6
o1 --> c7
c6 --> e1
c7 --> e1
o1 -.-> g1
